# Translated 1:1 from src/main/resources/META-INF/accesstransformer.cfg — keep both files in sync.
# Entries are added together with the shared-source flip at gate M1 (field descriptors are
# derived from the resolved Minecraft 26.1.2 jar).
#
# Translation notes:
# - AT `public-f`/`protected-f` => accessible/mutable. Where the member is already public
#   (Slot.x/y) only `mutable` is emitted; where it is protected and only the final flag was
#   stripped (imageWidth/imageHeight) only `mutable` is emitted to keep protected visibility,
#   matching the AT exactly.
# - AT `protected` on private methods that AE2 overrides or super-calls from subclasses
#   (isHovering, getHoveredSlot, setUnderwaterMovement) => `extendable` (yields protected,
#   non-final). `accessible` would make them public *final* and break AEBaseScreen's
#   isHovering override.
# - AW has no "protected" target for plain access widening; AT `protected` entries that are
#   only *called* (not overridden) and AT `public` entries both map to `accessible`
#   (=> public). protected->public is a strict widening and is safe.
# - OMITTED: `protected AbstractContainerScreen.extractSlot(GuiGraphicsExtractor,Slot,II)V`
#   — already protected in the vanilla 26.1.2 fabric jar (the AT entry is a no-op there);
#   AE2's overrides in AEBaseScreen/MEStorageScreen are declared public and compile as-is.
#   If a future MC version narrows it, re-add as `extendable method`.

